<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Jan-March home aluminium sales up 14.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil Jan-March home aluminium sales up 14.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian internal sales of all primary aluminium reached 51,100 tonnes in January to March, up 14.1 percent on the 44,800 tonnes sold in the same period in 1996, said the Brazilian Aluminium Association (ABAL).</p>
<p>Sales in March reached 17,400 tonnes, up 17.6 percent from 14,800 tonnes in March last year and a rise of four percent on the 16,700 tonnes sold in February 1997.</p>
<p>ABAL expects the market to stabilise over the coming months, with monthly sales of around 18,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
